 40,000 students is the oldest Catholic university in the world.","grounding":[{"source":"wikivoyage","title":"Leuven","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Leuven","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"short":"Leuven is a lively university city in Belgium. Leuven Town Hall and Museum M come first on the list, and Park Abbey rewards the extra walk beyond downtown. Transport is good, and ten hours from May to September takes in the rest.","short_src":"rewrite","facts":{"population":101032,"visit_h":7.4}},"highlights":[{"id":"hl-st-peter-s-church-leuven","name":"St. Peter's Church, Leuven","kind":"Church","lat":50.87944,"lon":4.70111,"dist_km":0.0,"rank_score":7.33,"resolved_by":"catalogue","image":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/42127_Pieterskerk.jpg/960px-42127_Pieterskerk.jpg","author":"Johan Bakker","licence":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licence_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:42127_Pieterskerk.jpg","w":4464,"h":3583,"ok_print":true}}],"do":[{"name":"DOCVILLE International Documentary Film Festival","type":"activity","sources":["wikidata","wikivoyage"],"evidence":{"method":"open","n_sources":2,"sources":["wikidata","wikivoyage"],"curated":"wikivoyage_do"}},{"name":"International Short Film Festival Leuven","type":"activity","sources":["wikidata","wikivoyage"],"evidence":{"method":"open","n_sources":2,"sources":["wikidata","wikivoyage"],"curated":"wikivoyage_do"}},{"name":"Rock Werchter","type":"activity","sources":["wikivoyage"],"evidence":{"method":"open","n_sources":1,"sources":["wikivoyage"],"curated":"wikivoyage_do"}},{"name":"Sports","type":"activity","sources":["wikivoyage"],"evidence":{"method":"open","n_sources":1,"sources":["wikivoyage"],"curated":"wikivoyage_do"}},{"name":"Oud-Heverlee Leuven","type":"activity","sources":["wikivoyage"],"evidence":{"method":"open","n_sources":1,"sources":["wikivoyage"],"curated":"wikivoyage_do"}},{"name":"Bears Leuven","type":"activity","sour